\section{Dataset}

\dataset{} is built from ICLR 2020--2023, 2025, and 2026 using the latest rebuttal-version paper wherever available. We balance accepts and rejects within each year, yielding a balanced corpus with XX training samples and XX test samples.

\textbf{Data Availability.} OpenReview exposes submissions from several ML conferences, but artifact availability is highly uneven across venues and years. We therefore choose the years with the strongest joint availability of anonymized submitted-paper copies and public rejected submissions. In practice, this makes ICLR 2020--2023 and 2025--2026 the only viable basis for a large-scale accept/reject corpus built from rebuttal-era artifacts, while ICLR 2024 must be excluded because accepts are camera-ready and rejects remain rebuttal-era. Yellow cells in Table~\ref{tab:artifact_availability} mark the year/artifact combinations used in \dataset{}.

