\caption{\textbf{Example 1 (A$\to$R):} Neural PDE paper with human mean rating 2.0. Without the prior, the agent accepts with a generic weakness about missing baselines. With the SFT prior, it correctly identifies the narrow experimental scope (only two 1D PDEs)---the same core criticism raised by human R2: ``only 1D Advection and Burgers equations are used.'' The rating drops from 6 to 3, closely matching human consensus. Judge weakness identification improves from 4 to 5.}
\label{fig:review_example_1}
\end{figure*}

